menu "esp32-air-sound"

    config AIRSOUND_TONE_ENABLE
        bool "Send a test tone instead of silence when nothing streams"
        default n
        help
            Bench aid: a 1 kHz tone gated 0.5 s on / 0.5 s off. Off in normal use.

    config AIRSOUND_TONE_DB
        int "Test tone level, dB below full scale"
        range 0 60
        default 20

    config AIRSOUND_LINE_TRIM_DB
        int "Output trim, dB below full scale, applied to everything"
        range 0 40
        default 14
        help
            The PCM5102 puts out 2.1 Vrms at full scale, the Si4713 line input clips at 636 mVpk.
            Until a resistor divider sits in the aux path this digital trim keeps the transmitter
            out of its limiter. The trim is applied in 32-bit arithmetic on the way to the DAC.

endmenu
